{
  "type": "say",
  "text": "Thank you, Mr. Brooks and Ms. Green. Mr. Brooks, this is a fourth critical gap that must be addressed. The LMS being offline from 8:00 to 11:00 a.m. means the plan's current approach of scheduling instruction through the LMS at 8:00 a.m. will not work for any student. I'm adding this as a required revision: instructional files must be distributed by email as downloadable PDFs and made available for printing by 7:30 a.m. tomorrow. Ms. Green, your suggestion to coordinate the printed packets with the downloadable PDFs at pickup sites is exactly right — that ensures both the 38 households without reliable internet and all students affected by the LMS outage have access to instructional materials. So to summarize, I now expect four updates before I sign the final plan: (1) Ms. Shah — replace bus-route meal delivery with on-site pickup at North and South Campuses, 11:00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m.; (2) Nurse Ruiz — add the staffed nurse hotline from 8:00 a.m. to 12:00 p.m.; (3) Ms. Green — printed learning packets and bilingual phone check-ins for the 38 households, coordinated with the PDF distribution; (4) Mr. Brooks — instructional files distributed by email as downloadable PDFs, available for printing by 7:30 a.m. Please all update your sections, and once the revised briefing packet is ready, I'll review and sign the final operating plan."
}
```

